'\" t
.TH ROFFSUB 7 @DATE@ "roffsub @VERSION@" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
roffsub \- a roff subset for manuals read in a terminal
.SH DESCRIPTION
A roffsub document is a man page.
Every roff program displays it: man, nroff, groff, mandoc.
It is also simple enough for small awk and C routines to render from inside a program's own binary or bash function, at the width of the terminal in use, with bold and italic where the terminal can show them.
One source then serves as the installed page and as the program's built-in help.
.PP
This page defines the source form, how it is rendered, and how a program presents it.
The form is checked; content is not.
